CONTEXT Migration IN ENGLISH
-- Step 2, the end of the copying, and the moment of transition.
-- Every pair of old.title is in new.title and registered in copyTitle.
-- The article promises that both transactional invariants of step 2 are satisfied (T_1)
-- and that the copying has terminated (eqn:copyingTerminates).
-- The new invariant authored is violated by b1 and b2; the migration system accepts that,
-- because there it is a business constraint (B_fix), so the system satisfies its invariants (eqn:satisfaction).
INCLUDE "../scripts/library_migration.adl"

POPULATION new.title[new.Book*new.Title] CONTAINS [ ("b1", "Emma") ; ("b2", "Ivanhoe") ]
POPULATION copyTitle[old.Book*old.Title] CONTAINS [ ("b1", "Emma") ; ("b2", "Ivanhoe") ]

RULE copiedIntoNew : old.title - copyTitle |- new.title
RULE copyRegistered : new.title /\ old.title |- copyTitle
RULE copyingTerminates : old.title = copyTitle

ENDCONTEXT
